A branch cannot be checked out in two worktrees simultaneously. If Git
permitted this, two independent indices would write competing updates
to the same reference file, corrupting history.

Attempting to check out an occupied branch yields:
    fatal: 'dev' is already checked out at '/path/to/tree'

The repository is a directed acyclic graph; branches are merely names
for vertices. Multiple branches can point to the same vertex, but one
branch name cannot belong to two working directories at once.

To liberate a branch, either switch the occupant to another branch,
detach its HEAD, or point a new branch name at the same commit.
